Calc: an .xlsx keeps the cached results of its filled-down (shared) formulas when it is opened.

The import set the cached number of a shared formula but left the cell dirty, unlike a formula of its own
(applyCellFormulaValues resets it). A dirty cell is calculated again by the first reader of its value, and the
optimal row height pass at the end of the import (ScDocShell::UpdateAllRowHeights, through
ScColumn::GetOptimalHeight -> HasEditCells -> GetRangeScriptType -> ScCellFormat::GetString) reads every cell. So a
large workbook of filled-down SUMIF/VLOOKUP/COUNTIF columns was calculated in full while loading, although formulas
are never recalculated on load by default (OOXMLRecalcMode = 1): a 24 MB synthetic workbook of 200 000 rows with
a SUMIF(B:B;B2;K:K) column took 160 s on 32 cores, and on a 4-core PC many minutes, looking like a hang. The same
workbook with every formula written out per cell (no shared formulas) opened in 24 s.

The shared path now resets the dirty flag as the non-shared path does. A document whose formula results are all 0
or missing is still recalculated in full (WorkbookFragment::recalcFormulaCells), and OOXMLRecalcMode "always" or
"ask" behaves as before.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
Test: CppunitTest_sc_subsequent_filters_test5 testXlsxSharedFormulaCachedResults (builds a small .xlsx whose
shared formulas carry cached results that differ from the calculated ones; fails without the fix);
tests/unit/test_large_file_open_patches.py.

--- a/sc/source/filter/oox/formulabuffer.cxx
+++ b/sc/source/filter/oox/formulabuffer.cxx
@@ -200,11 +200,16 @@
                             bHasCalculatedFormulaCells = true;
                         }
                         pCell->SetResultDouble(fVal);
-                        /* TODO: is it on purpose that we never reset dirty here
-                         * and thus recalculate anyway if cell was dirty? Or is it
-                         * never dirty and therefore set dirty below otherwise? This
-                         * is different from the non-shared case in
-                         * applyCellFormulaValues(). */
+                        // Keep the cached result, as applyCellFormulaValues() does for
+                        // a formula of its own: a cell left dirty is calculated again
+                        // by the first reader of its value, and the optimal row height
+                        // pass at the end of the import reads every cell. A large
+                        // workbook of filled-down (shared) formulas was then calculated
+                        // in full while loading although OOXMLRecalcMode is "never".
+                        // A document whose results are all 0 or missing is still
+                        // calculated in full (WorkbookFragment::recalcFormulaCells).
+                        pCell->ResetDirty();
+                        pCell->SetChanged(false);
                     }
                 break;
                 case XML_str:
